 WHERE slug = 'relume' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Relume is an AI tool that generates website briefs, sitemaps, and wireframes from a text description, backed by a component library for Webflow, Figma, and React. It also offers an in-beta Publish path that can host the finished site on a custom domain, in addition to exporting to Webflow or Figma for development.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'relume' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Relume is an AI-powered website planning and building tool aimed at agencies, freelancers, and designers. Describe a site's purpose and audience, and Relume generates a brief, a full sitemap, and detailed wireframes for each page, which can be customized before export or publishing. The product now spans two offerings: 'Build with Relume,' an AI website builder, and 'Site Builder,' a component-library-driven wireframing tool.

The company recently repositioned itself: it moved its primary domain from relume.io to relume.ai, and launched a 'Publish' path (currently in beta) that takes a project from brief to a live hosted site, with Relume handling the custom domain and SSL. This sits alongside the original 'Export' path, which now supports React (Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui) in addition to Webflow and Figma. Relume also ships a Library MCP for pulling components into other AI tools.

Key capabilities include AI-generated briefs, sitemaps, and wireframes, a style guide generator, unlimited collaboration, and a component library of 1,000+ pre-built sections (hero, features, pricing, FAQ, etc.) available across Webflow, Figma, and React. The free tier of Build with Relume includes free hosting on a relume.live subdomain; the free tier of Site Builder includes 30 Webflow components and 30 React components.

Pricing is split across the two products. Build with Relume has a free forever plan (no card required, limited shared AI usage, unlimited websites, relume.live hosting) and a Pro plan starting from $14/month with a premium AI model and priority access; hosting on a custom domain is priced separately, starting at $12/project/month. Site Builder has a free plan (30 Webflow + 30 React components) and paid tiers: Starter from $18/month, Pro from $40/month (1,000+ components across all platforms, up to 300 component storage), Team from $36/month per user with a 3-user minimum, and a custom-priced Enterprise tier. All published prices use a 'From $X/month' structure, so the final cost depends on configuration; no annual-billing discount is currently published.

Limitations: the Publish path is still in beta, and using it means the live site runs on Relume's own hosting rather than an existing platform. The Export path still requires a separate Webflow or Figma account for that workflow. Exact final pricing for any tier depends on usage and configuration rather than a single flat number.

Relume suits agencies, freelancers, and designers who want to accelerate the planning and wireframing phase of a web project, whether they intend to hand off to Webflow, Figma, or React, or publish directly through Relume's own beta hosting.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'relume' AND lang = 'en';

