UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Zed is a code editor built in Rust; its 1.0 release (April 29, 2026) introduced Parallel Agents, letting multiple AI agents work on different parts of a codebase at once. It offers a capped free Personal plan alongside paid Pro and Business tiers.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'zed' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Zed is a code editor built entirely in Rust, designed for low-latency, native performance instead of the Electron shell used by editors like VS Code and Cursor. Zed 1.0 shipped on April 29, 2026, marking five years of development and more than a million lines of Rust code.

The headline feature introduced alongside 1.0 is Parallel Agents (announced separately on April 22, 2026): users can run multiple AI agents at the same time, each working independently on a different part of the codebase, rather than waiting for one agent task to finish before starting another. Zed also built the Agent Client Protocol (ACP), a standard that lets external agents such as Claude Agent, Codex, OpenCode, and Cursor run inside the Zed editor. In August and September 2026 Zed announced and opened a public beta for Delta, a new product positioned as a replacement for pull requests: a multiplayer environment, backed by DeltaDB, for coding with agents and reviewing their output, running locally and in-browser via WebAssembly, and syncing with third-party agents like Claude Code.

Inside the editor, Zed gives access to models from Anthropic, OpenAI, and Google directly, without requiring separate API key setup for each provider.

Zed's Personal plan is free forever but caps Zed-hosted AI use at 2,000 accepted edit predictions; unlimited use requires bringing your own API keys or an external agent. The Pro plan costs $10 per month (USD) and includes unlimited edit predictions plus $5 in monthly tokens with usage-based billing beyond that, and comes with a 14-day free trial. The Business plan costs $30 per seat per month (USD) and adds org-wide AI model policies, data governance controls, unified spend visibility, and role-based access controls; it does not bundle a fixed LLM credit allotment, and order forms are available for 25+ seats.

As a 1.0 product, Zed's extension and plugin ecosystem is still smaller than VS Code's or JetBrains', and its Rust-native architecture means some VS Code extensions are not compatible. The new Parallel Agents feature can also produce coordination conflicts when multiple agents touch overlapping code.

Zed suits developers who want a fast, resource-efficient editor with real parallel AI agent capability, and teams that need published, centralized AI governance pricing without committing to a heavyweight enterprise tool.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'zed' AND lang = 'en';

